   "notes": "Exact implementation of equations (1)-(5) and the best-fit column of Table 6. The published fit fixes K300,0=261 GPa and K'300,0=4, uses alpha(T,0)=a0+b0*T-c0/T^2, integrates alpha exactly for V(T,0), and varies K(T,0) linearly with temperature. The printed a0 is derived, not independently refined: alpha(300 K,0)=1.7e-5 K^-1 constrains a0=1.7e-5-300*b0+c0/300^2. V0 was not a common absolute-volume fit parameter because each experimental block was normalized to its own ambient volume; 162.32(23) A^3 is the explicitly identified Run 1 ambient anchor used here to make the published normalized EOS executable. The thermal parameter errors in Table 6 are regression errors; the paper recommends the broader systematic interval dK_dT=-0.028+/-0.017 GPa/K. The experimental ranges report the 128 selected fit observations, not all measurements or an extrapolation guarantee.",
